From 48f686e4aafae12acb46a788bdf32bd78f5a42c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Primarosa <simone.primarosa@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:09:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat: configure minreplicas floors for elastic partial
 preemption

Partial preemption must not shrink an elastic workload below the minimum viable capacity required for execution. Workload minCount preserves its admission semantics, so preemption lower bounds must be tracked separately to prevent over-evicting worker groups during preemption cycles.

Introduce the kueue.x-k8s.io/reclaim-min-counts annotation and JobWithReclaimMinCounts interface. RayCluster and RayJob set worker group floors to minReplicas, while EnsureWorkloadSlices synchronizes floor metadata across active workload slices capped at each slice count.
